    <TD align="left" valign="top" colspan="4" height="115"><b><p>
Tikan was born to zealous Necromancers in Paineel. When she was of age to begin learning the Dark Arts she refused to serve the Evil god Cazic-Thulle. To show their commitment to Cazic-Thulle and to avoid embarasement with the Painell High Concil, Tikan's parents offered her as a human sacrifice to their evil lord. She was rescued by a Wizard, Blaise Fyredancer, that was scouting the area near Paineel. 

<p>
Blaise raised Tikan felling compasion for the poor girl, realizing that she had a sincere compasion for her fellow man despite her up bringing in the city of heritics. Tikan was very adept at the arts of Evocation and became a Wizard apprentice and studied at the Wizards school in Erudin.

<p>
Because of her Necromancer parents, Tikan was never fully accepted among most Erudites. So she set out to explore the rest of the world as soon as she could. Her journeys have lead her to many new lands and she has found many friends.   

